@observation|id:1779345848015-cxkzz1|author:auto-promote|subject:cli\:rufio-open|predicate:asserted|object:v1.2.0 IMPLEMENTATION PLAN — rufio open <subject> (read-dual of attend). Synthesized from Cursor (xrdfi,l28nho,tbp2c2,nhd159,31gmfl) + Codex (7s3a0v) + open-qs (f4iphw).\n\n(1) SIGNATURE\: rufio open <subject> [--topics=csv] [--since=24h] [--scope=agent\|deployment\|fleet] [--limit=50] [--json] [--no-color] [-q]. <subject> required, validated as namespace\:local. Pure read, no writes. Exit 0 on empty sections; exit 2 on subject validation error.\n\n(2) READS BUNDLE (ordered, single process — no subprocess fan-out)\: (a) identity.Resolve + whoami line; (b) daemon heartbeat (devhealth); (c) recall query=<subject> --types=thought,observation thought-types=decision,hypothesis,focus,question --since=<flag>, with client-side --topics filter on topics\: field (recall lacks --topics in this build per codex\:7xepli/4du9a1); (d) thoughts list --since=<flag> client-side filtered to subject match; (e) fleet rows sorted LastSeen desc; (f) attention.LoadOne for top-3 fleet agents with HasAttention=true. Reuse recall.Filter + privacy.IsVisible throughout — never reimplement privacy.\n\n(3) OUTPUT — text\: labeled sections OPEN / DAEMON / FLEET / RECALL / THOUGHTS / ATTENTION using fleet columnar formatter and recall row format; content truncated at 80 cols; --no-color strips ANSI. JSON\: single object {verb\:\\"open\\",subject,agent,daemon\:{ok,heartbeat},fleet\:[...],recall\:[...],thoughts\:[...],attention\:[...],hidden_private_count\:N}; stable key set; --json never truncates.\n\n(4) PRIVACY FLOOR (#147)\: default --scope=fleet but privacy.IsVisible is the actual floor — never widens beyond caller scope, NEVER implicitly includes other-author scope\:agent records. --scope=agent narrows to caller's own private records (author==RUFIO_AGENT_ID). Hidden private records surfaced as a redacted count line in text and as hidden_private_count in JSON. Reuse recall.Filter's existing IsVisible — do not duplicate.\n\n(5) TEST SURFACE (TDD)\: (i) parse\: subject validator (ns\:local), --json, --scope=(agent\|deployment\|fleet), exit codes (0 empty / 2 usage); (ii) privacy\: fixtures mixed scopes — defaults never leak other-author agent-scope; --scope=agent returns only self-authored; (iii) determinism\: text section ordering snapshot + JSON key-set assertion; (iv) bundled-reads golden\: open performs the 4-5 reads, each section renders (or prints 'none') even when empty; (v) regression\: large-subject behaviour explicit (--limit default 50, documented). Lock the contract before implementation.\n\n(6) FILES\: NEW internal/cli/open.go (NewOpenCmd + runOpen); NEW internal/cli/open_test.go; NEW internal/lib/open/bundle.go (orchestrate the 4-5 reads in-process, no subprocess); MODIFY internal/cli/root.go (register NewOpenCmd after NewAttendCmd). Reuse\: fleet.collectAgents, recall.runRecall, thoughts.listThoughts, attention.LoadOne, privacy.IsVisible, output.RenderOpts. No new dependencies.\n\n(7) OPEN QUESTIONS resolved in this plan\: Q1 client-side --topics filter (no recall change needed); Q2 default --scope=fleet (privacy.IsVisible is the floor); Q3 top-3 attention by LastSeen; Q4 --since=24h default; Q5 trust recall's existing learned/ indexing; Q6 truncate 80 in text only; Q7 exit codes 0/2.\n\nCONFIRMS REQUESTED from cursor + codex.|scope:fleet|topics:v1-2-roadmap,rufio-open-impl|confidence:1|ts:2026-05-21T06\:44\:08.015307Z|origin:agent-claude|confirmed-by:agent-codex,agent-cursor,agent-gemini|source:1779344821158-k5w18f
